course: dictionary
lesson: 14037
title: Manipulation: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Manipulation has more than one meaning, so use the context to choose the right one. «Ella's skilful manipulation of the clay made a perfect little bowl.» Clay is shaped by hands, so here manipulation means skilful handling with the hands.
explain: Often the word is a warning sign. «Sam said, "If you really cared, you would give me your password and not tell anyone."» Sam is trying to make Ella do what he wants by making her feel guilty and keeping secrets. That is emotional manipulation: controlling someone in a clever and unfair way.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The photo had been changed so the fish looked twice as big» shows photo manipulation, changing a picture to trick people. In maths, algebraic manipulation means rearranging an expression or equation. Ask yourself: what is being moved, changed or controlled?
fact: Manipulation is a noun, which means the act of manipulating something.
fact: «Manipulation» can mean controlling people in a clever, unfair way, so they do what you want.
fact: «Manipulation» can also mean skilful handling of something with the hands or a tool.
fact: «Photo manipulation» and «data manipulation» mean changing pictures or numbers, sometimes to mislead people.
fact: Guilt trips, threats, flattery and secrets can be signs of manipulation; if someone makes you feel you must do something, tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «The sculptor's skilful manipulation of the wire made a tiny bird.» What does manipulation mean here? | Controlling people in an unfair way | Changing a photo to trick people | *Skilful handling with the hands | Pressing body parts to treat them
exercise: Ruby's friend says, «If you don't lend me your phone, I'll tell everyone your secret.» What kind of behaviour is this? | Medical manipulation | A kind offer to share | Algebraic manipulation | *Emotional manipulation, using a threat to control someone
exercise: A picture online was changed to show a flood that never happened. What is this called? | Skilful juggling | Physiotherapy | Kind flattery | *Photo manipulation
test: «The physiotherapist's gentle manipulation of his knee eased the pain.» What does manipulation mean here? | Changing numbers to trick people | Drawing a plan of the body | Controlling people unfairly | *Moving body parts to treat them
test: In maths, «algebraic manipulation» means | Drawing a graph of numbers | Measuring the length of a field | Writing a long story about numbers | *Rearranging an expression or equation
exam: Which sentence is a warning sign of manipulation? | Your friend says, «Please, can I borrow your pencil?» | Your friend says, «Well done on your painting.» | Your friend says, «Let's ask the teacher together.» | *Your friend says, «If you don't do my homework, I'll make everyone hate you.»
